<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n7133" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνάπᾰλιν</span></b> , Adv.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>back again,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰέναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Plt.</u>
					269d
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Phdr.</u>
				264
			</span></i>&lt;*&gt;, al.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπὶ τὸ πέρας ἢ ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>EN</u>
					1095b1
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. στραφῆναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Cael.</u>
					285a8
				</span></i>
			,  etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>over again,</i>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔμπαλιν</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Tht.</u>
				192d
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>contrariwise, on the opposite side,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Coac.</u>
				321
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. πορεύεσθαι</span> proceed
				<i>in reverse,</i> i. e. <i>wrong order,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Ti.</u>
				82c
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. τιθέναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>APr.</u>
					37b11
				</span></i>
			, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. ἐστιν ἡμῖν ἢ τοῖς
				ἄλλοις</span>
			<i>in the opposite way to</i> . . , <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>HP</u>
				8.3.5
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῖς πολλοῖς . . καὶ τοῖς
			ἀ.</span> (i. e. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῖς
			ὀλίγοις</span>) Teles<i><span class="en">
				p.15.9
			</span></i> H. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>IV.</b> in
			proportion, <i>inversely;</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ ἀ. λόγος</span> the <i>inverse</i>
			ratio <i><span class="en">
				Euc.
				5
			</span></i><i><span class="en">
				<u>Def.</u>
				13
			</span></i>.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. ἔχειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Cael.</u>
					273b32
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>conversely, An.Ox.</i><i><span class="en">
				4.325
			</span></i>.</div>
